    "methodology": "10,000-game solitaire heuristic. Sequencing: land drop, cheapest ramp, commander on affordability, biggest affordable threat, then other proactive spells. Meaningful board = pressure score >= 6 or 2+ threats. Lethal proxy = cumulative combat-pressure proxy >= 40; combat pressure uses mana-value-based creature scoring because card metadata omits power/toughness. Combo lethal = at least one winConditions[] entry tagged kind:'combo' has all pieces present (hand, battlefield, or substitutable) and combined mana cost payable. Substitution priority for missing pieces: (1) bargain free-cast tutor (e.g. Beseech the Mirror) when a non-rock enchantment is on battlefield OR commander has been in play for 1+ turn (approximates Sauron-style amass token from real-game opponent casts); (2) type-matched regular tutor whose tutor_targets includes piece's card type and tutor_mv_cap permits piece's MV; (3) reanimation spell (decklist[].primary_role/secondary_role == 'recursion') for permanent pieces only \u2014 cost replaces piece's cast cost (treats piece as if in graveyard). Each substitute is consumed once per combo line. Tutors, non-permanent combo pieces, and reanimation spells are reserved from filler casting. v2 limitations: no literal graveyard tracking (reanim assumes piece could be in GY), no opponent interaction, no multi-turn assembly tracking, no stack-trigger ordering. Commander copy-trigger engine modeled (DEC-393): with the commander on the battlefield, each instant/sorcery cast resolves one extra copy while 3 untapped creatures remain to tap (each use taps 3 for the turn \u2014 board-state gated, not always-on). Creature counts = creature permanents + a stat-less ledger of creature tokens from resolved spells (fixed counts only; X-spells and storm credit 0, so copy counts are floors). Copies re-credit draw and land-ramp but are not cast (CR 707.10) \u2014 they never re-trigger the engine."
